===== root =====
Surface repository-grounded divergence before code is accepted.

Usage: argot [COMMAND]

Commands:
  audit           Audit recent history for patterns that would have prompted review. It scores the surviving base-to-head change and classifies only explicit AI markers; informational, exits 0
  init            Set up argot for this repo: fit the voice model and report its health (`--suggest` lists directories you may want to exclude first)
  fit             Fit the voice model to this repo (train + calibrate, one-shot)
  check           Check code changes against the calibrated scorers
  rules           List every rule with its group and effective severity for this repo
  review          Score a PR (or diff range) against the local voice without checking it out
  voice-diff      PR-level out-of-voice metric plus ranked hot-spots for a ref/range. Informational: always exits 0 (use `check`/`review` to gate)
  inspect         Report corpus composition, calibration health, and repo suitability
  mute            Accept a finding: by hash for one hit, or `--path` for a standing rule covering a whole tree (appends a [[mute]] to argot.toml)
  list-mutes      List active suppressions across argot.toml [exclude], inline comments, and argot.toml [[mute]]
  review-mutes    Re-score muted files and report which suppressions no longer fire
  status          Show the current repository's argot state
  list            List all registered repositories
  update          Update the argot CLI to the latest release
  cache           Inspect or clear the machine-wide cache (`~/.cache/argot`): the downloaded model and the embedding cache
  uninstall       Remove argot from this machine: every repo's artifacts, the model cache, global state, and the binary (shows the full list first)
  mcp             Run a Model Context Protocol server for LLM coding agents (stdio)
  describe-voice  Generate a STYLE.md describing the repo's learned voice
  conventions     List the conventions this repo already follows — naming, syntax idioms, familiar imports, and typical calls by area — from the fitted model
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Docs: https://argot.tmonier.com/docs/
Coding agents: https://argot.tmonier.com/llms.txt
===== root-semantic =====
Surface repository-grounded divergence before code is accepted.

Usage: argot [COMMAND]

Commands:
  audit           Audit recent history for patterns that would have prompted review. It scores the surviving base-to-head change and classifies only explicit AI markers; informational, exits 0
  init            Set up argot for this repo: fit the voice model and report its health (`--suggest` lists directories you may want to exclude first)
  fit             Fit the voice model to this repo (train + calibrate, one-shot)
  check           Check code changes against the calibrated scorers
  rules           List every rule with its group and effective severity for this repo
  model           Manage the local embedding model behind the semantic rules
  review          Score a PR (or diff range) against the local voice without checking it out
  voice-diff      PR-level out-of-voice metric plus ranked hot-spots for a ref/range. Informational: always exits 0 (use `check`/`review` to gate)
  inspect         Report corpus composition, calibration health, and repo suitability
  mute            Mute a hit by hash (appends a [[mute]] to argot.toml)
  list-mutes      List active suppressions across argot.toml [exclude], inline comments, and argot.toml [[mute]]
