===== model =====
Manage the local embedding model behind the semantic rules

Usage: argot model <COMMAND>

Commands:
  fetch   Download and verify the model now (instead of on first use)
  status  Show whether the model is present, where, and its size
  clean   Delete the model cache (re-fetched on next use)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

===== model-fetch =====
Download and verify the model now (instead of on first use)

Usage: argot model fetch

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

===== model-status =====
Show whether the model is present, where, and its size

Usage: argot model status

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

===== model-clean =====
Delete the model cache (re-fetched on next use)

Usage: argot model clean

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

===== audit =====
Audit recent history for patterns that would have prompted review. It scores the surviving base-to-head change and classifies only explicit AI markers; informational, exits 0

Usage: argot audit [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --commits <COMMITS>  How many commits back to audit (first-parent line) [default: 50]
      --since <SINCE>      Audit everything since a date (YYYY-MM-DD) or a duration (90d, 12w, 6m, 1y)
      --format <FORMAT>    Output format: terminal, json, markdown, or html [default: terminal]
      --repo <REPO>        Path to the repository [default: .]
  -h, --help               Print help

===== init =====
Set up argot for this repo: fit the voice model and report its health (`--suggest` lists directories you may want to exclude first)

Usage: argot init [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --repo <REPO>      Path to the repository [default: .]
      --suggest          Don't fit — instead list directories you may want to add to `argot.toml [exclude].paths` first (statistical evidence only; you decide)
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format for `--suggest`: human (terminal) or json (stable, machine-readable — consumed by the setup skill) [default: human] [possible values: human, json]
  -h, --help             Print help

===== fit =====
Fit the voice model to this repo (train + calibrate, one-shot)

Usage: argot fit [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --repo <REPO>   Path to the target repository [default: .]
      --slice <SPEC>  Calibrate an extra threshold for a slice of the repo (repeatable): `path:<prefix>` (a subdirectory), `author:<email>`, or `auto` (one per top-level directory). Hunks in a slice are judged against its threshold
  -h, --help          Print help

===== check =====
Check code changes against the calibrated scorers

Usage: argot check [OPTIONS] [REFERENCE]

Arguments:
  [REFERENCE]  Optional git ref or range (e.g. abc1234 or a..b). Empty = workdir [default: ""]

Options:
      --repo <REPO>
          Path to git repository [default: .]
      --staged
          Check staged changes only
      --unstaged
          Check unstaged changes only
      --commit <SHA>
          Check a single commit
      --only <GLOB>
          Restrict to matching files (glob, repeatable)
      --exclude <GLOB>
          Drop matching files (glob, repeatable)
      --argot-dir <ARGOT_DIR>
          Directory containing argot artifacts [default: .argot]
      --hunk-lines <N>
          Hunk-body lines shown under each above-threshold hit (0 to suppress) [default: 6]
  -v, --verbose
          Show full hunk contents (no truncation; overrides --hunk-lines)
      --min-confidence <MIN_CONFIDENCE>
          Only show hits at or above this confidence tier [default: unusual] [possible values: unusual, suspicious, foreign]
      --rule <NAME=SEVERITY>
          Override a rule's severity for this run: `--rule <name>=<error|warn|off>` (repeatable; accepts rule or group names — see `argot rules`)
      --error-on-warnings
          Exit non-zero when `warn`-severity findings are present (CI strictness)
      --add-ignores
          Insert an inline ignore comment above every current finding instead of reporting (adopting argot on an existing codebase). Working-tree only
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human (terminal), json (stable machine-readable), sarif (SARIF 2.1.0 for code-scanning uploads), or github (Actions workflow commands → inline PR annotations). Machine formats write nothing but the document to stdout [default: human] [possible values: human, json, sarif, github]
  -q, --quiet
          Suppress informational stderr notes (model line, staleness nudges, suppression counts). Errors still print
  -h, --help
          Print help

===== rules =====
List every rule with its group and effective severity for this repo

Usage: argot rules [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  test  Run the fixture tests of this repo's custom rules (`.argot/rules/<name>/tests/<case>/{input.<ext>, expected.json}`)
  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --repo <REPO>      Path to the repository (its argot.toml decides the effective severities) [default: .]
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format: human or json [default: human] [possible values: human, json]
  -h, --help             Print help

===== rules-test =====
Run the fixture tests of this repo's custom rules (`.argot/rules/<name>/tests/<case>/{input.<ext>, expected.json}`)

Usage: argot rules test [OPTIONS] [NAME]

Arguments:
  [NAME]  Test one rule by name (default: every discovered rule)

Options:
      --repo <REPO>  Path to the repository (its argot.toml decides the effective severities) [default: .]
  -h, --help         Print help

===== review =====
Score a PR (or diff range) against the local voice without checking it out

Usage: argot review [OPTIONS] <TARGET>

Arguments:
  <TARGET>  A PR URL, `#number` / `number`, a `base..head` range, or a commit sha

Options:
      --repo <REPO>      Path to the local repository (whose fitted voice scores the PR) [default: .]
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format: human, json, sarif, or github (PR annotations) [default: human] [possible values: human, json, sarif, github]
  -h, --help             Print help

===== voice-diff =====
PR-level out-of-voice metric plus ranked hot-spots for a ref/range. Informational: always exits 0 (use `check`/`review` to gate)

Usage: argot voice-diff [OPTIONS] <TARGET>

Arguments:
  <TARGET>  A ref or `base..head` range to summarize (e.g. `main..HEAD`)

Options:
      --repo <REPO>      Path to the repository [default: .]
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format: human, json, markdown (a PR-comment / job-summary score card), shields (shields.io endpoint JSON for a README badge), or svg (a self-contained badge) [default: human] [possible values: human, json, markdown, shields, svg]
      --top <N>          Hot-spots to list [default: 10]
  -h, --help             Print help

===== inspect =====
Report corpus composition, calibration health, and repo suitability

Usage: argot inspect [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]  Path to the repository to inspect [default: .]

Options:
      --model            Inspect the fitted model artifact (hashes, provenance, and the typical callees per cluster) instead of repo suitability
      --top <N>          Typical callees shown per cluster under `--model` [default: 8]
      --corpus           List the files that would shape the voice, one per line, and exit. The same walk `fit` uses — a corpus preview that needs no fit
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format: human (terminal) or json (stable machine-readable) [default: human] [possible values: human, json]
  -h, --help             Print help
===== mute =====
Accept a finding: by hash for one hit, or `--path` for a standing rule covering a whole tree (appends a [[mute]] to argot.toml)

Usage: argot mute [OPTIONS] [HASH]

Arguments:
  [HASH]  Hit hash from `argot check` output (the `[abc123def456]` on a hit line). Mutes exactly that hit — a per-hit acceptance, not a standing rule: the same finding in a sibling file gets its own hash. Omit it and pass `--path` instead for a durable, pattern-scoped mute

Options:
      --path <GLOB>      Mute by path glob instead of by hash (`src/legacy/**`) — a standing `[[mute]]` that covers every future hit under it, not one hash
      --rule <RULE>      Narrow a `--path` mute to one rule or group (e.g. `foreign-import`). Without it the mute covers every rule on those paths
      --reason <REASON>  Why this hit is muted (recorded in argot.toml [[mute]])
      --expires <DAYS>   Auto-expire the mute after N days (e.g. `30d`)
  -h, --help             Print help
===== list-mutes =====
List active suppressions across argot.toml [exclude], inline comments, and argot.toml [[mute]]

Usage: argot list-mutes

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

===== review-mutes =====
Re-score muted files and report which suppressions no longer fire

Usage: argot review-mutes [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --prune  Remove the dead mutes — those whose file is gone (rewrites argot.toml [[mute]])
  -h, --help   Print help

===== status =====
Show the current repository's argot state

Usage: argot status [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --repo <REPO>      Path to the repository to report on [default: .]
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format: human (terminal) or json (stable machine-readable) [default: human] [possible values: human, json]
  -h, --help             Print help

===== list =====
List all registered repositories

Usage: argot list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format: human (terminal) or json (stable machine-readable) [default: human] [possible values: human, json]
  -h, --help             Print help

===== update =====
Update the argot CLI to the latest release

Usage: argot update

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

===== cache =====
Inspect or clear the machine-wide cache (`~/.cache/argot`): the downloaded model and the embedding cache

Usage: argot cache [COMMAND]

Commands:
  clear  Delete the embedding cache (and, with --all, the downloaded model)
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

===== cache-clear =====
Delete the embedding cache (and, with --all, the downloaded model)

Usage: argot cache clear [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --all   Also remove the downloaded embedding model (re-fetched on next use)
  -h, --help  Print help

===== uninstall =====
Remove argot from this machine: every repo's artifacts, the model cache, global state, and the binary (shows the full list first)

Usage: argot uninstall [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --dry-run  Show everything that would be removed, remove nothing
      --yes      Skip the confirmation prompt (required when not on a terminal)
  -h, --help     Print help

===== mcp =====
Run a Model Context Protocol server for LLM coding agents (stdio)

Usage: argot mcp [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --repo <REPO>  Path to the repository whose fitted voice the server scores against [default: .]
  -h, --help         Print help

===== describe-voice =====
Generate a STYLE.md describing the repo's learned voice

Usage: argot describe-voice [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --repo <REPO>  Path to the repository [default: .]
      --top <N>      Typical callees listed per cluster [default: 8]
      --out <FILE>   Write to this file instead of stdout (e.g. `STYLE.md`)
  -h, --help         Print help

===== conventions =====
List the conventions this repo already follows — naming, syntax idioms, familiar imports, and typical calls by area — from the fitted model

Usage: argot conventions [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --repo <REPO>      Path to the repository [default: .]
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format: human (terminal) or json (stable machine-readable) [default: human] [possible values: human, json]
      --top <N>          Callees listed per cluster and idioms listed per language [default: 8]
  -h, --help             Print help
